  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25600168",
      "title": "Using Redux Data in React Components",
      "sourceHash": "12b833a4ca16c4bce92285cc2822cefdedd608ad8a2ddc6bba10a80c4e89e79d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.12,
          "end": 4.41,
          "en": "Let's say we wanna utilize",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.41,
          "end": 8.5,
          "en": "this provided store not in the app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.5,
          "end": 12.1,
          "en": "but in the counter component which I rendered there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.1,
          "end": 16.3,
          "en": "That's this counter component in the components folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.3,
          "end": 19.32,
          "en": "We got more components there we'll use them later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.32,
          "end": 21.4,
          "en": "for the moment it's the counter component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.4,
          "end": 23.39,
          "en": "that matters to us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.39,
          "end": 25.89,
          "en": "Now that's the component you're seeing on the screen here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.89,
          "end": 28.15,
          "en": "when you're running your Def server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.15,
          "end": 31.05,
          "en": "It shows us basically a container",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.05,
          "end": 34.21,
          "en": "where we wanna output the counter value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.21,
          "end": 37.3,
          "en": "We got a toggle counter button for hiding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.3,
          "end": 38.853,
          "en": "or showing the counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.93,
          "end": 44.54,
          "en": "Now here I wanna start by outputting the current counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.54,
          "end": 48.67,
          "en": "And for this we need to get access to our Redux store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.67,
          "end": 50.17,
          "en": "and to the data in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.17,
          "end": 55.17,
          "en": "And we again do that with help off the React Redux Library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.83,
          "end": 60.36,
          "en": "So from React Redux we again wanna import something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.36,
          "end": 65.36,
          "en": "and the something which we are importing is a React Hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 66.23,
          "end": 70.33,
          "en": "A custom hook made by the React Redux team.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.33,
          "end": 73.333,
          "en": "The use selector hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.21000000000001,
          "end": 78.48,
          "en": "There also is use store hook, which we could use as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 78.48,
          "end": 81.37,
          "en": "which gives us direct access to the store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 81.37,
          "end": 84.9,
          "en": "but you as selector is a bit more convenient to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 84.9,
          "end": 89.55,
          "en": "because that allows us to then automatically select a part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 89.55,
          "end": 93.22999999999999,
          "en": "of our state managed by the store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 93.22999999999999,
          "end": 95.68299999999999,
          "en": "So I will use use selector here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 96.62,
          "end": 99.97999999999999,
          "en": "Now if we would be using a class-based component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 99.97999999999999,
          "end": 103.3,
          "en": "and not a functional component as we are here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 103.3,
          "end": 105.99000000000001,
          "en": "and as we are in the majority of the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 105.99000000000001,
          "end": 109.62,
          "en": "then there also is a connect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 109.62,
          "end": 111.65,
          "en": "which we could use instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 111.65,
          "end": 115.21000000000001,
          "en": "This function can be used as a wrapper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 115.21000000000001,
          "end": 119.1,
          "en": "around our class component to connect that class component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 119.1,
          "end": 120.07,
          "en": "to the store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 120.07,
          "end": 122.3,
          "en": "I'll come back to that later for the moment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 122.3,
          "end": 124.593,
          "en": "we'll focus on use selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 125.71,
          "end": 129.12,
          "en": "So here in this functional component we can now get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 129.12,
          "end": 133.853,
          "en": "to the data managed in our store by using use selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 135.29,
          "end": 139.27,
          "en": "We call this and now we need to pass a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 139.27,
          "end": 141.2,
          "en": "to use selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 141.2,
          "end": 145.34,
          "en": "A function which will be executed by a React Redux",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 145.34,
          "end": 148.78,
          "en": "of function which then basically determines which piece",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 148.78,
          "end": 151.593,
          "en": "of data we wanna extract from our store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 152.68,
          "end": 155.48,
          "en": "Of course at the moment we have a very simple state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 155.48,
          "end": 158.91,
          "en": "Just an object with a counter property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 158.91,
          "end": 160.73,
          "en": "But in bigger applications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 160.73,
          "end": 164.52,
          "en": "you will have more complex states with tons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 164.52,
          "end": 168.95,
          "en": "of different properties maybe nested objects and arrays",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 168.95,
          "end": 172.27,
          "en": "and therefore being able to just get a slice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 172.27,
          "end": 175.67000000000002,
          "en": "just a tiny part of that overall state object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 175.67000000000002,
          "end": 178.25,
          "en": "in a easy way is worth a lot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 178.25,
          "end": 180.76,
          "en": "And that's what use selector allows us to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 180.76,
          "end": 182.91,
          "en": "For this we should pass a function to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 182.91,
          "end": 185.99,
          "en": "a function of which we'll receive the state managed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 185.99,
          "end": 190.49,
          "en": "by Redux and then we return the part of the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 190.49,
          "end": 191.8,
          "en": "which you wanna extract.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 191.8,
          "end": 194.053,
          "en": "So here for example, state stock.counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 195.19,
          "end": 199.75,
          "en": "Again this function will be executed for us by React Redux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 199.75,
          "end": 201.94,
          "en": "It will then pass the Redux state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 201.94,
          "end": 204.66,
          "en": "so the manage the data into this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 204.66,
          "end": 207.488,
          "en": "when it executes it and then basically executes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 207.488,
          "end": 210.73,
          "en": "this code to retrieve the part of the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 210.73,
          "end": 212.89,
          "en": "which you need in this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 212.89,
          "end": 216.54399999999998,
          "en": "And then use select or therefore overall gives us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 216.54399999999998,
          "end": 218.27,
          "en": "that returned value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 218.27,
          "end": 220.32999999999998,
          "en": "So we get a counter constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 220.32999999999998,
          "end": 223.653,
          "en": "which is the counter managed by Redux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 224.54,
          "end": 228.6,
          "en": "Now the great thing is that when you use use selector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 228.6,
          "end": 232.51,
          "en": "React Redux will automatically set up a subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 232.51,
          "end": 236.32999999999998,
          "en": "to the Redux store for this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 236.32999999999998,
          "end": 238.69,
          "en": "So your component will be updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 238.69,
          "end": 241.92,
          "en": "and will receive the latest counter automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 241.92,
          "end": 245.69,
          "en": "whenever that data changes in the Redux store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 245.69,
          "end": 247.73,
          "en": "So it's an automatically reactive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 247.73,
          "end": 250.56,
          "en": "and changes to the Redux store will cause",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 250.56,
          "end": 253.83,
          "en": "this component function to be re executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 253.83,
          "end": 256.28,
          "en": "So you always have the latest counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 256.28,
          "end": 259.48,
          "en": "That's why use selector is a very useful hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 259.48,
          "end": 261.97,
          "en": "and why it is the hook we use for getting data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 261.97,
          "end": 262.973,
          "en": "out of the store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 264.07,
          "end": 267.26,
          "en": "If you ever would unmount this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 267.26,
          "end": 270.44,
          "en": "if it would be removed from the DOM for whatever reason,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 270.44,
          "end": 274.02,
          "en": "React Redux would also automatically clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 274.02,
          "end": 275.88,
          "en": "the subscription for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 275.88,
          "end": 279.623,
          "en": "So it manages that subscription for you behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 281,
          "end": 284.22,
          "en": "Now that we got this counter, we can use it down there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 284.22,
          "end": 288.673,
          "en": "to output the counter value like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 289.65,
          "end": 294.65,
          "en": "And if we now save this, we therefore now see zero here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 295.62,
          "end": 300.49,
          "en": "And that's how we can get access to data managed by Redux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 300.49,
          "end": 304.24,
          "en": "Of course the question now is how we can change that data?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 304.24,
          "end": 306.583,
          "en": "How can we dispatch actions?",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}